<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Required by Apple since 1 May 2024 for any app that calls a required-reason
	API. This file is the in-binary counterpart of two other statements, and all
	three have to agree or App Review treats the mismatch as the answer:

	  1. App Store Connect → App Privacy → "Data Not Collected"
	  2. docs/landing/privacy.html (pages.kubepilot.org/privacy.html)

	NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty on purpose. The app has no analytics,
	crash-reporting or advertising SDK and no backend of ours: credentials stay
	in the Keychain, and cluster data, logs and AI requests go only to the
	KubePilot server the user configured. We never receive any of it, which is
	what "not collected" means in Apple's definition.

	Cluster data does leave the device — to the user's own server, and onward to
	whatever AI model that server's operator configured. That is disclosed and
	consented to in KubePilot/Core/Privacy/AIConsent.swift, not declared here,
	because the recipient is the user's own infrastructure rather than ours.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<!-- AIConsent stores the user's AI data-sharing answer per account, and
		     AuthManager / KubePilotAPI remember which cluster an account last
		     selected. Both are this install's own state; nothing is read back
		     out of the app and no other app or SDK can see it. -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
